et,_Vieille_Cour,_22_rue_Quincampoix_-_Getty_Museum.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/30233816","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2013-12-19 11:31:35","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Old Courtyard, 22 rue Quincampoix","source":"commons-desc-page"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Rue de Seine (Paris)|Rue de l'\u00c9chaud\u00e9 (Paris)|Artworks without Wikidata item|Photographs in The J. Paul Getty Museum|Artworks with known accession number|CC-PD-Mark|Photographs of Paris by Eug\u00e8ne Atget|Files from the Getty's Open Content Program|1912 photographs of Paris|1908 photographs of Paris|PD-old-95|Photographs by Eug\u00e8ne Atget in the J. Paul Getty Museum|Triangular buildings in Paris|Images of Paris from the Getty Museum","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Eug%C3%A8ne_Atget\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Eug\u00e8ne Atget\"><span title=\"French photographer (1857-1927)\">Eug\u00e8ne Atget</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Residents surrounding this narrow passageway provided few signs of their domestic lives for the photographer to record. Baskets and a few rags hang out of the uppermost window, while two people below observe Eug\u00e8ne Atget making this picture. On a windowsill to the right, houseplants bask in the sunlight invading the tall shaftway. Although people inevitably ambled in and out of this courtyard, dropping off and picking up their ironing at \"the most pleasant ironers,\" the absence of activity when this picture was created conveys a stark sense of gloominess. The weather-beaten facades and the rubbish bins at the left further underscore this impression. During the time that it took to record the details of this space on Atget's glass plate negative, the brightness of the sunlight from the street outside caused overexposure of the view through the portal.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1908 or 1912","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.getty.edu/art/collection/object/40280\">The Getty Center, Object 40280</a>\n</p>\n<table style=\"width:100%; clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; background-color: var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f9f9f9); color: var(--color-base, #202122); border: 2px solid var(--border-color-muted, #dadde3); border-spacing: 8px; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0;\" lang=\"en\" class=\"layouttemplate licensetpl\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:100px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:J._Paul_Getty_Museum\" title=\"J. Paul Getty Museum\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Getty_Center_2.jpg/120px-Getty_Center_2.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Getty_Center_2.jpg/250px-Getty_Center_2.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"400\" data-file-height=\"600\"></a></span>\n</td>\n<td><i>This image was taken from the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:J._Paul_Getty_Museum\" title=\"Commons:J. Paul Getty Museum\">Getty Research Institute</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.getty.edu/about/opencontent.html\">Open Content Program</a>, which states the following regarding their assessment that <b>no known copyright restrictions</b> exist:</i>\n<dl><dd>Open content images are digital surrogates of works of art that are in the Getty's collections and in the 